    "customer_notice_days": 3,
    "scope": "confirmed_incidents",
    "during_investigation_required": null,
    "phase_in_months": 0,
    "quote": "Manufacturers must report every confirmed thermal incident involving overheating, smoke, fire, or thermal injury to the relevant regulator within 24 hours of becoming aware of it, including incidents initially reported by customers or service personnel. Manufacturers must notify affected customers within 72 hours when an incident presents a credible safety risk to their unit or household, and provide follow-up instructions promptly."
